WEBVTT

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:04.290
Winter approaches

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:24.540
How did it go?

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.580
No use. It's completely shut up.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.090
Yeah, it's the same on this side.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.550
Chako! We're going home for now!

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:40.480
Got it! Be right down!

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.540
They're cold too, I guess.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.210
Tell me 'bout it. They don't move even if you surprise 'em.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.410
But I can't believe how quickly it got so cold!

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.080
It was so hot until a little while ago!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.490
Cold!

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.260
Then don't just stand there, move your hands!

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.930
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.210
I get it!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.800
Pague...

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.760
He's awfully energetic considering how cold it is.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.000
Howard!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.100
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.030
This is all?

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.200
Kaoru!

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.300
Did you find anything?

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:19.330
That's all?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.640
Even one is something.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.580
That's why I said to leave it to me

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:35.580
Howard!

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.530
Yeah, yeah, your majesty.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.500
Hey!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.900
We're home!

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.740
Luna!

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.800
Cold, cold!

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.080
Cold!

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:57.800
Were you a good boy?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.530
Pague ate.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.260
Yes, you were giving Pague leaves.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.440
I see. You couldn't get inside after all.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.360
We thought we might get it to open somehow.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.810
I thought it might be a little warmer inside.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.100
We still have hope.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:26.300
Those ruins don't seem to be completely shut down.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.610
What do you mean?

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.550
Something was blowing out of the top at an amazing rate.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.430
What do you mean, "Something"?

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.810
We don't know that yet.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:39.610
I took a sample 'cuz I was curious, so we can try analyzin' it.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:46.330
It doesn't seem like we can get into the ruins soon, so I guess we have to stay here for a while.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.280
It does seem so.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.080
We can't stay here!

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.700
It'll get colder from now on.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.500
The cold won't be bearable here.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:57.350
Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.750
How do you know that?

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.850
The clouds get thicker every day.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:05.110
And fruit has stopped growing on the trees.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.030
Winter is approaching.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.380
Winter?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.490
The clouds certainly seem to be getting thicker...

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.040
..but I wonder if it will really get any colder than this.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:17.940
I have no doubt.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.600
We should find a cave and move into it as soon as possible.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.140
A cave?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.090
Don't be ridiculous!

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:28.480
Why do we have to go to a cave, when we finally have Everyone's House built?

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.390
But if it gets any colder than this...

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.010
That's why we made cloaks!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.680
When the real winter comes, just cloaks won't suffice.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:40.360
Bell...

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:41.830
It's the truth.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.640
We should find a cave and move into it as soon as possible.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.450
That's a thing to say all of a sudden.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.080
What should we do, Luna?

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.840
Does it have to be a cave?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.880
If we just need to counteract the cold, we could improve Everyone's House...

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.980
That won't work!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.030
But it won't be that easy to find a cave.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.830
I know of a cave.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:08.600
Really?

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:12.010
If you want to give it a look, I can show you the way.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:13.700
Luna.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:16.890
But...

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.330
Isn't it okay just to look?

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.330
Let's go there tomorrow.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:25.480
Tomorrow?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:27.460
The sooner the better.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:29.640
No helping it.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.300
But we're only going to look!

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:48.690
It's over there.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.130
I guess it's no good after all.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.280
The ground's pretty rugged too.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:06.160
And it seems somehow creepy.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:06.760
Yes...

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.350
No, this would be perfect.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.790
It's wide enough, and a river flows right nearby.

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.360
We won't have to worry about drinking water.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.630
Hey, hey. Are you serious?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.930
That might be true, but it's so humid.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.680
If we take out the moss and let the wind through, it should be fine.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.830
But with the ground this way, we won't have anywhere to sleep.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:32.450
We can loosen the stones and flatten it out.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.730
The ceiling is suited to ventilation as well.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:40.810
If we make a vent opening there and slope the ceiling, we can have a fire inside.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.080
It should be warmer than Everyone's House.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.980
This place will be fine. We'll make it through the winter.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.980
We're not talking about some daydream here.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:54.130
Loosen the rocks and make a vent hole?

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.260
How much time do you think that's going to take?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.380
If we have that much free time, we should spend it looking for food!

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.110
I agree with Howard.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.740
We gather less and less every day.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:08.790
For now, I think we should gather any little bit more food that we can.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.060
Everyone...

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.730
We should forget about it after all.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:14.380
Luna...

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.010
Okay.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.380
In that case, I'll work on this place alone.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:21.460
Bell...

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.150
Leave him, leave him!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.590
If he wants to do it, let him do it!

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.130
But...

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:33.010
Luna...

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:34.780
Let's go.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:35.830
Right...

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:46.330
Alright...

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.730
Don't tell me this stuff clumps together.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.160
What is it?

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.830
The first is the analysis.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.090
I wonder how Bell is doing.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.210
Only two fish?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:48.090
Menori, what about fruit?

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:50.380
Sorry.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:56.640
If I don't eat fruit once in a while and recharge my Hydrogen, my body will stop movin'!

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.440
Tomorrow, tomorrow!

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.440
If they have no bread, then let them eat cake!

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.700
I wonder if Bell is okay.

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:08.000
Just this much?

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:09.240
Put up with it.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:14.230
We haven't been able to find food in a week.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.710
I can only believe it's going to get worse from now on.

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.010
Chew thoroughly before swallowing.

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:32.320
There's no cake either!

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:38.980
You couldn't sleep either?

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:41.680
Y-yeah...

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.310
It's gotten colder here right before our eyes.

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:49.480
Maybe what Bell said was correct after all.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:51.460
Perhaps.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:55.780
But I don't think we can forgive Bell's actions.

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:00.010
Food decreases day by day.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.880
Even if it's just one more person, we need his help.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.840
I know. I'll go talk to him tomorrow.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.360
Bell, are you here?

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:32.790
Bell...

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:34.480
Luna...

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.530
Bell...

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:43.360
So the smoke will get out through here.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:48.280
And this is to keep the heat from escaping as much as possible.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:53.150
But it's amazing to think you did this all by yourself.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.110
Kaoru helped me out as well.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.610
Kaoru did?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:02.230
I see, Kaoru did.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.630
Well, I'll...

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.030
Bell!

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:10.480
Don't push yourself. You have to rest a little.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.430
You haven't been sleeping properly, have you?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.860
I can rest any time.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.100
But...

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.390
There's a reason I can't rest!

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.090
Bell!

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.440
How are you?

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:36.130
I'm fine now.

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:37.700
Thank you.

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:43.550
Can I ask you something?

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:47.300
What did you mean by a reason you couldn't rest?

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.900
That planet was covered in snow all year round.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:01.250
Dad was there to mine mineral resources.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:07.330
It was about three months after we moved there.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:12.910
It suddenly got cold, and the sky was covered in dark clouds.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.290
What's wrong?

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.290
No, nothing.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.680
But Dad knew.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:33.500
A terrible cold wave would come soon.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.240
We can't leave things as they are!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.890
We need to reinforce and secure the lifelines!

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:43.030
Secure the lifelines?

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:46.360
In the best of times we're exhausted. Who's going to do that?

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:50.260
And house-building isn't our job.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.740
We might get hurt doing unnecessary work like that.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.460
It seems pretty stupid to us.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:57.050
If you want it done so much, do it yourself!

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.580
Dad tried desperately to convince them...

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.540
...but he couldn't change anyone's mind.

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:13.210
Starting that day, Dad worked on the lifelines while everyone else was asleep.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.680
Disconnecting the water pipes, insulating the heating systems...

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:23.490
And just like Dad had said, a violent cold snap arrived.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:29.710
The blizzard continued for days, and the temperature reached seventy below zero.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:35.790
The water pipes burst, and the heating systems shut down one after another.

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:43.060
But the heating systems and water pipes Dad had prepared against the cold made it through safely.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.940
If Dad hadn't done anything back then...

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.730
After two weeks, the cold snap let up.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.110
Thank you.

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:06.090
It's all thanks to you.

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.830
We're really sorry about the terrible stuff we said to you.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:10.740
Dad!

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.650
Even now, I remember...

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:24.800
...the warmth of Dad's calloused hand, and his proud face.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.610
Bell, your dad was great.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.160
So I'll do it.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.750
No matter what anyone says, I'll do it.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.740
And protect everyone from the cold, just like Dad did!

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:52.630
What? Help Bell?

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:55.210
What about our work here?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:56.940
Of course we'll do that too.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.190
We'll help Bell once we're done.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:01.740
But if we do that, we'll be exhausted.

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:03.280
I'll be fine.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.610
Do what you want! Yeesh!

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.390
Just don't expect me to come with you!

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:24.200
Luna!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:28.550
Adam... Everyone!

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.630
That's pretty impressive!

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:34.400
I can't believe this is that same cave!

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.480
It gives me a very bright feeling!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.590
We might be able to live here comfortably after all!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:41.490
Yes.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:45.580
When we start a fire inside, it'll be far warmer than Everyone's House.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.000
Menori...

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:57.310
How much longer do you think it will take?

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.010
It should be fine after another week.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.990
So you mean if we all work on it, it'll be done in a day?

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:05.530
Menori!

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.140
Let's all do it together!

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.010
I'll help too!

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:13.960
Everyone...

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.630
I won't be beat.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.630
I'll hurry up on the analysis!

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:22.060
What? Everyone's helping Bell?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.530
Why not take a look?

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:26.410
Who'd go to a place like that?

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:29.190
Do as you like.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:30.950
Where are you going?

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:33.280
Sleep.

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.440
Don't scare me like that.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.810
They look like they're having so much fun.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.730
You're late.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.030
I'm not... really...

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:11.560
Howard!

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:17.900
I figured it out!

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:24.050
Infrared inhibitor particles?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.290
No doubt 'bout it.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:28.180
That's why it keeps getting colder.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:30.460
What do you mean?

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:34.250
This substance reflects the sun's rays.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:37.930
Of course, just one or two would be no big deal.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:41.150
But those ruins are gushin' out gobs of the stuff.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:46.400
So basically, those clouds are masses of these infrared inhibitor particles.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:49.960
It's like it's raising an umbrella over this island.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.430
Umbrella?

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.230
But why are the ruins doing it?

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:00.840
I don't know that.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:05.000
All I know is it'll keep gettin' colder from now on.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.340
Then Bell was right after all.

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:11.490
It would be best to hurry the completion of the cave.

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.460
Yes.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.050
Howard, will you help us too?

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.090
I have no choice.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:22.810
I have no idea when you'd get it done without me.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:24.990
Thank you, Howard.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.130
Then let's get right to work!

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:28.290
Yeah!

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:53.410
With this, we're done.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.060
Yeah.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:56.410
We're finished over here too.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:06.840
You did it, Bell.

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:08.380
Yeah.

00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:19.700
Dad...

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:26.980
It's not half bad.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:31.060
I can hardly believe we built it by ourselves.

00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:38.600
It's snow.

00:22:40.030 --> 00:22:40.890
Snow?

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:45.430
This is snow?

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:47.110
It's pretty.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.740
Snow! Snow!

00:22:51.650 --> 00:22:52.700
Snow!

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:55.550
The real winter is beginning.

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:06.650
Pague's becoming less energetic with the cold.

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:09.050
He seems happy when he's with Adam...

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:10.780
...but what should we do?

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:11.980
Actually, Luna...

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:16.100
...we found somethin' amazin' in the Eastern Woods!

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:17.790
What?

00:23:18.050 --> 00:23:19.960
Tada! It's...

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:21.880
Pague's Paradise!

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:23.880
Pague's Paradise?

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:28.180
Next time: I don't want to say goodbye.
